course: dictionary
lesson: 464
title: Armpit: a body word, and a rude one
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word armpit is made of two parts: arm and pit. A pit is a small hollow, and your armpit is the hollow place under your arm where it joins your shoulder. Armpits is the plural, so you have two of them.
explain: Read this: «Around puberty special sweat glands in the armpits switch on; their sweat is not smelly until bacteria eat it, which is why a wash helps.» The clues are sweat, smelly and wash. They tell you the armpit is a body part that needs washing, so you can work out the meaning before you check a dictionary.
explain: Be careful: armpit can also be informal and rude. A place called «the armpit of» somewhere is its ugliest or least pleasant part. The rest of the sentence gives the clue. If the words around it sound unkind, the meaning is probably rude too. Swap in your meaning to test it.
fact: An armpit is the hollow place under your arm where it joins your shoulder.
fact: Sweat glands in the armpits make sweat, and bacteria eating that sweat is what makes it smell.
fact: A wash helps keep armpits fresh, and older children may use deodorant.
fact: A thermometer can be held in the armpit to measure temperature, as in «a digital thermometer in the armpit or ear».
fact: Informal: «the armpit of» a place means its least pleasant part, so it is a rude way of talking about somewhere.
exercise: Your armpit is the hollow place under your arm where it joins your shoulder. Where is your armpit? | Inside your ear | On your knee | On the top of your head | *Under your arm, near your shoulder
exercise: In «checks his skin, including behind his knees, in his armpits and in his hair», which word is the plural of armpit? | hair | knees | *armpits | skin
exercise: Why might someone hold a thermometer under your arm? | To measure how tall you are | To wash your hair | *To check your temperature | To count your steps
test: If someone says a town is «the armpit of» the county, what do they mean? | Its tallest tower | Its best park | *Its least pleasant part | Its newest school
test: Why does washing your armpits help? | It makes sweat grow bigger | It makes your arm longer | It stops your armpits being part of your body | *It removes the sweat that bacteria would eat
exam: Read «Ticks ... bite to drink blood ... a boy hiking checks his skin, including ... in his armpits and in his hair, after the walk.» Why does he check his armpits? | To count his freckles | To find a lost sock | To see if his arm is still there | *To look for ticks that might bite him
